<h1>about</h1>

<p>Hello, my name is Joe.</p>

<p>For as long as I can remember, I have had an interest in taking things apart, figuring out how they work, and putting them back together.
It started with Nerf guns as a kid, then DIY electronics projects in high school, and then cars when I was old enough to drive (and could afford it).</p>

<p>In high school, I had a slow (Celeron), basic (economy), boring laptop which I learned all kinds of things about. I went through some Codeacademy, 
experimented with Linux distros, and more. My senior year of high school, I built my first tower PC with the help of my great uncle and a local Microcenter.
Little did I know what I was getting myself into... I've built at least four computers for myself, as well as a few computers for friends.</p>

<p>I believe that's what makes my skills unique. Whether it's tearing apart and rebuilding a pump, troubleshooting a complex die set, replacing a gear set on 
a gearmotor? I can do that.
Finding out why the automated assembly equipment stopped; whether it means diving into ladder logic of the PLC, looking at sensors, maybe a solenoid is stuck? 
I can do that too.</p>

